{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And at the crossing (ואל)</b> — the place where roads branch off from it, to say to the Babylonites: Which way did the fugitive go?" "<b>And do not shut up his survivors (ואל תסגר שרידיו)</b> — to hand over, as though you shut him in."], :book :obadiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "The lemma reads ואל from ואל־הפרך in Obadiah 1:14; the word פרך is understood as a crossing/fork in the road."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Obadiah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=18&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:20:32.261942773Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}